1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,251
This republic lasted about eleven hundred years.

2
00:00:03,471 --> 00:00:05,406
Then it voted itself out of existence

3
00:00:05,406 --> 00:00:06,309
in a single day.

4
00:00:06,779 --> 00:00:09,236
The Most Serene Republic of Venice ruled

5
00:00:09,236 --> 00:00:11,591
the Adriatic and traded from Cyprus to

6
00:00:11,591 --> 00:00:12,155
Flanders.

7
00:00:12,625 --> 00:00:16,022
In 1797 Napoleon's army reached its borders

8
00:00:16,022 --> 00:00:19,220
and he demanded that the government step

9
00:00:19,220 --> 00:00:19,686
down.

10
00:00:20,156 --> 00:00:21,264
On the 12th of May,

11
00:00:21,264 --> 00:00:22,460
the Great Council met.

12
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:26,336
Only 537 of about 1,200 members came,

13
00:00:26,336 --> 00:00:28,205
not even a quorum.

14
00:00:28,675 --> 00:00:30,510
512 voted yes.

15
00:00:30,730 --> 00:00:32,612
The last doge, Ludovico Manin,

16
00:00:32,612 --> 00:00:34,390
took off his cap of office,

17
00:00:34,390 --> 00:00:36,063
and the republic was over.

18
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:39,160
Five months later, Napoleon handed Venice to

19
00:00:39,160 --> 00:00:41,483
Austria in the Treaty of Campo Formio.

20
00:00:41,953 --> 00:00:44,253
His soldiers even took the bronze horses

21
00:00:44,253 --> 00:00:45,643
of Saint Mark to Paris.

22
00:00:45,863 --> 00:00:48,487
They came back in 1815.

23
00:00:48,957 --> 00:00:50,685
Should a republic have fought instead?

24
00:00:50,905 --> 00:00:53,149
Comment below, and follow for more lost

25
00:00:53,149 --> 00:00:53,721
countries.

